invariant: INV-16
file: sha3.h
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh
reason: sha3_on_instructions answers yes where the session's ch_cfg.cpu
  leaves CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA3 clear, so a session runs ML-KEM's
  hashes on the SHA-3 instructions that its caller never said the CPU has
  or runs in constant time, and dies of SIGILL on a CPU without them.
  Every key and secret is still right on a CPU with them. The qemu lane
  builds the two loops with clang for arm64 and runs them on cortex-a72,
  which has no FEAT_SHA3, where the rows without the bit must pass. The
  lane skips without docker, and this then reports unguarded rather than
  caught.

--- old
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA3) != 0;
--- new
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA3) == 0;
